# The example extension open-tasks (installed in the empty home by tests/drive.rs) keeps a count
# of open tasks in the status line, the graph's too. The graph runs in the menu's loop, so the
# extension is answered while it is open: a task another program writes shows in the count at
# once, without leaving the graph.
size 140x30
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
env COLD_LAVA_TODAY=2026-11-07
wait-for ☐ 16 open tasks
keys g
wait-for example-workspace · 39 nodes
expect ☐ 16 open tasks
write Inbox/Chores.md - [ ] Sweep the ash off the roof\n
wait-for ☐ 17 open tasks
expect example-workspace · 40 nodes
keys q
wait-for cold-lava workspaces
expect ☐ 17 open tasks
keys q
exits 0
